# Data — never commit, each teammate downloads independently. Anchored to
# repo root (leading /) — a bare "data/" would also match every module's
# 00N_Module/data/ (a real directory here, holding just a documentation
# stub — see the note below), which is a different thing entirely and
# needs to stay tracked.
/data/
InitialData/
*.fastq.gz
*.vcf
*.vcf.gz
*.vcf.gz.tbi
*.bam
*.bai
*.cram
*.fasta
*.fa
*.fa.fai
references/

# Container images — rebuild locally, don't version large binaries
*.sif
*.img

# Challenge/organizer materials tied to the dataset — treat like input data,
# each teammate keeps their own local copy instead of versioning it.
Challenge_*.docx

# results/ — internal working output only, never tracked. This covers every
# module's results/ under Re-calling_Pipeline/, VCF_pipeline/, and the
# top-level rollup dir, at any depth. Reverses an earlier convention (this
# project used to track manifests + small QC reports as the run record);
# results/ derives from real patient sample data, so none of it — reports,
# logs, or manifests — goes in version control, full stop. Keep only the
# empty .gitkeep placeholders so `git clone` recreates the expected
# directory skeleton.
**/results/*
!**/results/.gitkeep

# 00N_Module/data — these are symlinks (just a path string) or plain
# documentation stubs (see each module's data/README.txt), not the data
# itself, so they ARE tracked; the real files they point at are already
# excluded above (InitialData/, references/).

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
env/

# OS
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/

# Nextflow
.nextflow/
.nextflow.log*
work/